As expected, FT-only improves fluency relative to extractive RAG, while generative RAG partially mitigates this gap through language-model generation. The hybrid model consistently yields the highest BLEU, ROUGE-L, and chrF scores across all subsets. This demonstrates that retrieval does not degrade generation quality when combined with fine-tuned reasoning, and in fact enhances lexical and semantic alignment on dynamic and mixed questions.
